# trica-agent: where to send the inventory (docs/reference/agent.md, "Sending to a server").
# Read by the systemd unit (EnvironmentFile). Nothing here is a secret: the enrolment
# token is a file, referenced by path, never a value in this file.
#
# With no server set, the agent keeps the latest batch in /var/lib/trica-agent/batch.json
# and sends nothing.
#
# Server: https://host:port of the transport listener (transport.addr of `trica server`).
#TRICA_AGENT_SERVER=https://trica.example.com:8443
#
# CA certificate of the server (the public ca.pem of transport.ca_dir), copied here
# out of band. Readable by the trica-agent user.
#TRICA_AGENT_CA_FILE=/etc/trica-agent/ca.pem
#
# Enrolment token, in a file readable by the trica-agent user: a one-time token for
# agent:<this host's name>, or a class token for a fleet (trica enrol create --prefix
# agent, ADR 0035), the same file on every host (install -m 0640 -o root -g
# trica-agent). Read only while the host has no certificate (in /var/lib/trica-agent);
# once enrolled it can be deleted.
#TRICA_AGENT_ENROL_TOKEN_FILE=/etc/trica-agent/enrol-token
#
# Metrics of the spool, for the node exporter's textfile collector (docs/reference/agent.md,
# "Metrics"). The unit can only write below /var/lib/trica-agent: give it the textfile
# directory with a drop-in (ReadWritePaths=) first.
#TRICA_AGENT_METRICS_FILE=/var/lib/node_exporter/textfile_collector/trica-agent.prom
